    "result_text": "Both findings addressed, build green (2/2 tests pass).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 duplicated SHA-256\u2192hex boilerplate (agreed).**\nExtracted a single shared helper `HashUtils` in the existing `util` package:\n- `HashUtils.sha256Hex(seed)` \u2014 full lower-case 64-hex digest.\n- `HashUtils.sha256UpperHex(seed, length)` \u2014 first `length` upper-case hex chars, implemented as `sha256Hex(...).substring(0, length).toUpperCase()`.\n\nAll three call sites now route through it:\n- `Owner.getIdentityKey()` \u2192 `HashUtils.sha256Hex(...)` (removed the private `Owner.sha256Hex` and its now-unused `MessageDigest`/`NoSuchAlgorithmException`/`StandardCharsets` imports).\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.computeHouseholdId` \u2192 `HashUtils.sha256UpperHex(..., 12)`.\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.hash8` \u2192 `HashUtils.sha256UpperHex(..., 8)`; removed the local `sha256UpperHex` and the three now-unused crypto imports.\n\nThe crypto boilerplate now lives in exactly one place.\n\n**Finding 2 \u2014 orphaned `existsOwnerInHousehold` + stale doc (agreed).**\nRemoved the method from both `ClinicService` (interface) and `ClinicServiceImpl` (impl), along with its stale \"single basis for the household-duplicate rule\" Javadoc \u2014 that rule is retired now that duplicate detection is the single identity key. It had no remaining callers.\n\n**Non-blocking note on `soundex`/`soundexDigit` placement** \u2014 I agree and left them as static methods on `Owner`, consistent with the existing `fiscalYear`/`toBusinessDay` utilities there and used by both `getIdentityKey` and the service.\n\nAll acceptance behaviour is unchanged: the identity key still hashes `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`, `computeHouseholdId`/`hash8` produce byte-identical output to before (same algorithm, same case, same truncation), and the test suite is green.",
